{"id":"pirsig-zen-1968","title":"Pirsig: Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance","who":"Robert M. Pirsig and his son Chris","when":"July 1968, 17 days","vehicle":"Honda CB77 Super Hawk","kind":"moto","color":"#0f766e","media":[{"kind":"book","title":"Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance","by":"Robert M. Pirsig"},{"kind":"book","title":"Zen and Now","by":"Mark Richardson","note":"Retraces the ride forty years on"}],"summary":"The most-read motorcycle book ever is really a philosophy book. Pirsig and his 11-year-old son ride from Minnesota across the Dakotas and Montana, where their friends the Sutherlands turn back, then over the Rockies and through Idaho and Oregon to the California coast. Along the way: carburettor jets at altitude, the \"classical\" and \"romantic\" ways of seeing, and the ghost of his former self, Phaedrus. The Honda is now in the Smithsonian.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Zen and the Art of Motorcycle Maintenance","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zen_and_the_Art_of_Motorcycle_Maintenance"},{"label":"Psybertron: the ZMM route in detail","url":"https://www.psybertron.org/zammroutedetails.html"},{"label":"Smithsonian: the Zen motorcycle, 50 years on","url":"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smithsonian-institution/zen-motorcycle-still-inspires-philosophical-road-trippers-50-years-later-180984143/"}],"approximate":"Towns from route studies of the book; roads between them are approximate.","km":3965,"bbox":[-124.2161,37.7875,-93.0892,46.8776],"stops":[{"name":"St Paul","place":"Saint Paul, Minnesota","at":[44.9497,-93.0931],"date":"July 1968","text":"Father, son and the Sutherlands on a BMW leave the Twin Cities heading west on back roads.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Honda_Superhawk_305cc_CB77_1965._Light_years_ahead_of_anything_else._Those_were_the_great_days_of_early_Japanese_bikes%2Ceven_if_I_preferred_the_earlier_Super_Dream_-_Flickr_-_mick_-_Lumix.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg","page":"Honda Super Hawk","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honda_Superhawk_305cc_CB77_1965._Light_years_ahead_of_anything_else._Those_were_the_great_days_of_early_Japanese_bikes%2Ceven_if_I_preferred_the_earlier_Super_Dream_-_Flickr_-_mick_-_Lumix.jpg","credit":"Mick from Northamptonshire, England","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Oakes","place":"Oakes, North Dakota","at":[46.1386,-98.0904],"text":"Flat prairie and thunderstorms on the first day.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Klein_and_Sutmar_Block.jpg/500px-Klein_and_Sutmar_Block.jpg","page":"Oakes, North Dakota","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klein_and_Sutmar_Block.jpg","credit":"Andrew Filer","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Ellendale","place":"Ellendale, North Dakota","at":[46.0028,-98.527],"text":"Breakfast stop on day two, the start of the long talks about \"Quality\".","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Downtown_Ellendale%2C_North_Dakota_6-11-2009.jpg/500px-Downtown_Ellendale%2C_North_Dakota_6-11-2009.jpg","page":"Ellendale, North Dakota","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Ellendale%2C_North_Dakota_6-11-2009.jpg","credit":"Andrew Filer from Seattle (ex-Minneapolis)","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0"}},{"name":"Lemmon","place":"Lemmon, South Dakota","at":[45.9408,-102.1593],"text":"Across the open Dakotas.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kokomo_and_Boss_Cowman_Square.jpg/500px-Kokomo_and_Boss_Cowman_Square.jpg","page":"Lemmon, South Dakota","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kokomo_and_Boss_Cowman_Square.jpg","credit":"John Lee Lopez","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Miles City","place":"Miles City, Montana","at":[46.407,-105.8478],"text":"The engine runs rich with the altitude: new jets and a valve adjustment, the famous lesson in fixing your own machine.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Miles_city_2008.jpg/500px-Miles_city_2008.jpg","page":"Miles City, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miles_city_2008.jpg","credit":"Larry D. Moore","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Laurel","place":"Laurel, Montana","at":[45.6691,-108.7715],"text":"Towards the mountains.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Laurel%2C_Montana.jpg/500px-Laurel%2C_Montana.jpg","page":"Laurel, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laurel%2C_Montana.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Bozeman","place":"Bozeman, Montana","at":[45.6794,-111.044],"text":"Where Phaedrus once taught writing at the college. The Sutherlands head home from Montana."},{"name":"Missoula","place":"Missoula, Montana","at":[46.8701,-113.9953],"text":"Father and son continue alone.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg/500px-Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","page":"Missoula, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Lolo Pass","place":"Lolo Pass, Idaho","at":[46.635,-114.58],"text":"A night camped on a logging road at the pass."},{"name":"Cambridge","place":"Cambridge, Idaho","at":[44.5726,-116.6761],"text":"South through Idaho towards Oregon."},{"name":"Bend","place":"Bend, Oregon","at":[44.0582,-121.3153],"text":"Across the high desert of central Oregon.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/20210803_03_Bend%2C_Oregon.jpg/500px-20210803_03_Bend%2C_Oregon.jpg","page":"Bend, Oregon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20210803_03_Bend%2C_Oregon.jpg","credit":"David Wilson","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Eureka","place":"Eureka, California","at":[40.8019,-124.1708],"text":"Down to the Pacific coast of northern California.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Humbol